# Server history checkpoints, 2026-10-18

RTX 5050 Laptop GPU (8 GB, 40 W limit), Ryzen 7 host, packed
`/home/mitali/models/Qwen3.5-4B-Q8`, CUDA INT8 group 128, context 512,
temperature 0, SSE, 32 output tokens. One release-build server process per
variant, warm model, three sequential ON/OFF pairs per workload; no competing
CPU benchmark. An ON pair sends `marin_session_id: "new"` then the returned ID;
an OFF pair omits it. Each turn-two request includes the exact turn-one
assistant text. TTFT is first nonempty SSE content delta; decode is nonempty
SSE content events per second after the first, a proxy rather than formal
engine token/s. Total includes the final SSE chunk. `marin_reused_tokens` is
the number of earlier tokens skipped, excluding history advanced this turn.

Coding first user prompt: `("Explain Rust ownership, borrowing, lifetimes and
Send/Sync with a practical example. " * 8).strip()`; follow-up: `Now write
one small Rust function that illustrates borrowing.` Chat first user prompt:
`("Explain how to plan a two-day visit to Kyoto while minimizing travel time
and keeping costs low. " * 8).strip()`; follow-up: `Now adapt that plan for
rainy weather and a vegetarian traveler.`

