Greedy turn-one and turn-two text matched ON/OFF in all six pairs in each
variant. The first coding prompt tokenized to 177 prompt tokens, 170 stable
history tokens. The chat history reused 186 tokens. The official template
diverges before the prior assistant reply because Qwen3.5 adds the
non-thinking generation header, so generated-token state cannot simply be
kept. The checkpoint is taken after the exact rendered history prefix is
advanced and before the generation marker; generated-token commits remain
the ordinary decode loop, with no post-reply commit pass.

One baseline coding pair was profiled with temporary timers and GPU event
stages, then the instrumentation was removed. Rendering took 10–23 us and
tokenization 0.3–1.1 ms. The post-reply history rebuild took 1.328 s for
170 tokens and 1.758 s for 222 tokens. Ordinary generation took
2.198/1.248 s on turns one/two, including
1.370/0.480 s prompt passes and 8.7/9.1 ms sampling; the remaining decode
work already commits generated tokens as needed. There was no separate
post-reply generated-token commit to remove. GPU stage times for the two
rebuilds:

| Stage | 170 history tokens | 222 history tokens |
|---|---:|---:|
| QKV projections | 303.85 ms | 412.63 ms |
| MLP | 672.04 ms | 872.46 ms |
| DeltaNet recurrence | 236.73 ms | 318.70 ms |
| Output projection | 100.16 ms | 133.66 ms |
| Convolution | 4.74 ms | 5.69 ms |
| Full attention | 4.31 ms | 7.84 ms |
| KV writes | 0.135 ms | 0.163 ms |
| State transaction copy | 0.312 ms | 0.348 ms |

Each rebuild launched 523 kernels, made 72 device allocations and downloaded
993,280 logit bytes. Host `sync_wait` was 1.184/1.553 s, chiefly waiting for
queued model computation; it must not be added to GPU stage times. D2D copy
bytes are not exposed by current counters. The 4B config implies 51 MiB of
DeltaNet recurrent/convolution buffers per checkpoint; GPU KV uses 64-token
pages in eight-page slabs. Admission also counts the cloned page table and
split-attention scratch, then retains 512 MiB free GPU slack. The extra cache is transient during generation and
not persisted for another session. A 0.2 s `nvidia-smi` sample during an
additional coding pair saw at most 4536 MiB process VRAM. After each of the
three measured coding pairs, process RSS was 275,960 KiB and VmHWM 891,848
KiB; process VRAM readings were 4504–4536 MiB, a 32 MiB spread. The replay
chat server was observed at 4536 MiB process VRAM and 275,976 KiB RSS after
its three pairs. This is process-attributable sampled VRAM, not a continuous
device peak or an energy measurement.

The real 4B CUDA INT8 checkpoint test compared exact recurrent and KV state
before mutation, after branching and after restoration, then checked
continuation logits under the existing model tolerance. The pinned HF case
still passed (max logit difference 1.31e-5, max layer difference 1.18e-5,
normalized max 3.879e-6, relative RMS 3.288e-6; exact token choice). A real
server changed-prefix request reused zero positions and matched fresh greedy
output; closing a stream and retrying the same bearer ID matched fresh output
with 69 positions reused; issuing `new` evicted the prior ID (404).
After adding KV scratch to checkpoint admission, one final release-build
coding smoke pair remained correct: checkpoint 3.363 s versus fresh 4.518 s,
170 positions reused, identical greedy text, 275,996 KiB RSS and 4504 MiB
process VRAM. It is a confirmation run, not part of the three-run medians.

Reproduce with `cargo build --release -p cli --bin marin --locked` and
`target/release/marin --model /home/mitali/models/Qwen3.5-4B-Q8 --backend
cuda --quantize int8 --ctx 512 --temp 0 serve --port 8000`. Send the two
messages above as OpenAI-compatible streamed chat completions with
`temperature:0,max_tokens:32`. Repeat with `marin_session_id:"new"` on turn
one and the returned ID on turn two, then without the field for fresh runs.
Use `/proc/$PID/status` for RSS and `nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps=pid,used_gpu_memory
--format=csv,noheader` for process VRAM. The pinned reference command is
`target/release/marin-run verify /home/mitali/models/Qwen3.5-4B-Q8 --backend
cuda --quantize int8 --reference bench-results/qwen35-4b/hf-int8-128.json`.


# Gate text moved verbatim from BENCHMARKS.md (V7 consolidation)

## End-to-end session checkpoint gates (set before implementation)

On the same Qwen3.5-4B packed INT8 artifact, RTX 5050, context 512 and
temperature zero, use three matched two-turn coding pairs and three chat
pairs, with the exact returned assistant text in turn two. Compare reuse off,
the replay-based server, and the candidate on a warm model with no competing
benchmark. Accept only if greedy text and the pinned HF logit tolerances stay
unchanged; template boundaries, changed-prefix fallback, rollback,
cancellation, isolation and streaming/non-streaming equality pass. The median
whole-pair response time must improve at least 10% over reuse off and 20%
over replay-based reuse. Turn-two TTFT must remain at least 20% below fresh;
decode event rate must stay within 5% of replay-based reuse. Process RSS and
VRAM after three pairs may grow less than 128 MiB; checkpoint allocation must
respect the existing admission slack. Reject the candidate if any of these
gates fails. Archive raw timings and the measured breakdown separately.
